    ('34274', 1, $$Sun and Moon had to stop their fight to solve the flood chaos.$$),
    ('34274', 2, $$Sun and Moon helped the animals out of the flooded house.$$),
    ('34274', 3, $$The Sun chatted with the Moon.$$),
    ('34274', 4, $$The sun bade goodbye to the water. The sun bade good bye to Moon.$$),
    ('34274', 5, $$The rainbow stretched in the sky.$$),
    ('34274', 6, $$The children skipped and played.$$),
    ('34274', 7, $$The animals said hello to the moon.$$),
    ('34285', 0, $$Once upon the time, an old man who owns a 60-year-old clothing store enters a pizza shop next to his shop and sits at a table. A waiter put a glass of water in front of him.$$),
    ('34285', 1, $$How much for a slice of pizza? " "One dollar," answered the waiter. the man wears his glasses and counts a number of coins in it.$$),
    ('34285', 2, $$"How much for a slice of pizza? " the old man asked again. Some people are now waiting to get a table and the waiter starts to get a little impatient.$$),
    ('34285', 3, $$"1 dollar ...! " said the servant harshly. the old man counted the coins again, and finally said "I want to buy a slice of pizza," he said.$$),
    ('34285', 4, $$while waiting for the pizza, the old man sat at the dinner table. Not long after his cellphone rang. And it turns out it was his wife who was new from the city ... so happy, he accidentally dropped a flower pot that above the dining table$$),
    ('34285', 5, $$The waiter brought a slice of pizza the old man ordered, put the bill on the table and walked away leaving the old man.@When the old man was ordering pizza ...$$),
    ('34285', 6, $$After the old man finished eating pizza, he paid for it at the cashier and returned to his shop.$$),
    ('34285', 7, $$When the waiter comes back to clean the table, he starts wiping the table and then swallows hard because of what he sees. On the table, placed neatly next to an empty plate, 3 dollars worth, for replace the flower and pots.$$),
    ('34359', 0, $$There are shoes for all occasions.$$),
    ('34359', 1, $$Shoes for when the sun shines go 'flip-flop'.$$),
    ('34359', 2, $$Shoes for ladies at a party go 'clip-clop'.$$),
    ('34359', 3, $$Shoes for girls and boys at school go 'tough-turf'.$$),
    ('34359', 4, $$Shoes for daddies at work go 'shift-shaft'.$$),
    ('34359', 5, $$My favourite shoes are quiet and clean. Not like my brother's noisy, muddy boots!$$),
    ('34359', 6, $$My favourite shoes are prettier than my sister's smelly running shoes. My favourite shoes are for when I am relaxing.$$),
    ('34359', 7, $$These are the shoes I wear at home. They are soft. They hug my feet and go 'fush-fush'.$$),
    ('34414', 0, $$Once upon a time, there were two kingdoms. One kingdom in the South, and one in the North.$$),
    ('34414', 1, $$The rulers of these kingdoms used ravens to send messages to each other.$$),
    ('34414', 2, $$One day, the king of the Northern kingdom sent a message to the Southern kingdom.$$),
    ('34414', 3, $$The raven took the message and went home to her family. They read the message together.$$),
    ('34414', 4, $$The Northern king was declaring war on the South! The ravens discussed this and decided to change the message.$$),
    ('34414', 5, $$The raven delivered the new message to the Southern king.$$),
    ('34414', 6, $$The message was: Let peace prevail among us. The king smiled and sent the same message back to the Northern king.$$),
    ('34414', 7, $$To this day, the kingdoms are at peace. And no one knows that ravens can read.$$),
    ('34418', 0, $$This is Sam. He is cooking popcorns. His father asked him,"Sam, what are you doing? " "Why are you cooking popcorns? "Sam answered, "I am sorry father, I know I have done wrong". Sam's popcorns had spilled all over the kitchen.$$),
    ('34418', 1, $$"Father I want to know how to cook popcorns, my friend Ray knows how to cook, can you show me father? " Father answered, "Yes I will but first eat the ones you have cooked. Don't repeat that again, you could have burnt yourself".$$),
    ('34418', 2, $$The following day, father showed Sam how to cook popcorns. They cooked a lot and Sam carried some to school to share with his friends. Sam friends were very happy. "Sam can we come to your house so that your father can show us how to cook? "$$),
    ('34418', 3, $$Sam answered them, ,"yes I will ask my father". Sam's friends were very happy.$$),
    ('34418', 4, $$When Sam got home in the evening, he asked his father if he could show his friends how to cook popcorns and he agreed. They agreed with Sam and his friends to cook popcorns on the following Saturday.$$),
    ('34418', 5, $$Sam's friends were shown how to cook popcorns by Sam's father and they were all very happy.$$),
    ('34450', 0, $$In the faraway veld in Ncwadi, there was a frog who lived in the grass with her three children.$$),
    ('34450', 1, $$Every day, Mummy Frog went out to look for food for her family. Mummy Frog always warned her children, "Do not go outside while I am away! "$$),
    ('34450', 2, $$But the littlest frog wanted to know where her mother went to find food. One day, while Mummy Frog was away, Little Frog went out into the world.$$),
    ('34450', 3, $$Little Frog met a cow. She asked, "What do you eat? " The cow mooed, "I eat hay and grass. " "Where can I find them? " asked Little Frog. "Go down the road," replied the cow.$$),
    ('34450', 4, $$Little Frog met a pig. She asked, "What do you eat? " The pig oinked, "I eat vegetables and mealie pap. " "Where can I find them? " asked Little Frog. "Go down the road," replied the pig.$$),
    ('34450', 5, $$Little Frog met a cat. She asked, "What do you eat? " The cat meowed, "I eat meat. " "Where can I find it? " asked Little Frog. "Go down the road," replied the cat.$$),
    ('34450', 6, $$Little Frog met a snake. "What do you eat? " she asked. "I eat frogs," hissed the snake.$$),
    ('34450', 7, $$Little Frog jumped up high into the air. She jumped as fast as she could, all the way home. Little Frog did not look back.$$),
    ('34544', 0, $$After a night of heavy rain, a group of friends were on their way to school. They came to the river they had to cross every day. "Yoh! It's stopped raining, but look how full and fast the river is," said Siya.$$),
    ('34544', 1, $$"Oh no," groaned Linda. "Do you think teacher will be angry if we miss our classes today? " Linda remembered what the Sea Rescue instructor had taught them in water safety lessons. "Never cross a flooded river. Even if you can't get to school," the instructor had said.$$),
    ('34544', 2, $$Meanwhile, Lungi stepped straight into the river! "I know where the stepping stones are! " he yelled. But he soon fell into the water and the strong river began pulling him away.$$),
    ('34544', 3, $$"Run and get help! " shouted Linda. "Tell them to call the free emergency number 112, like the Sea Rescue lady told us. " "Help, help! " shouted Lungi as he struggled to keep his head above the water.$$),
    ('34544', 4, $$"Hold on, Lungi! " shouted Phelelani, as he grabbed a branch that he could use to help his friend. Phelelani's class had been taught that they should never go into the water to help someone as they might also be washed away.$$),
    ('34544', 5, $$Luckily, Lungi could float. He managed to grab the branch that Phelelani held out to him. Phelelani pulled Lungi to the safety of the river bank.$$),
    ('34544', 6, $$The children walked back to Lungi's home with him. He was soaking wet but relieved to be alive. His mother was very thankful that he was safe. "Thank you! " she said to Phelelani. "You saved my boy because you knew what to do! "$$),
    ('34544', 7, $$Lungi's father hugged his son. "I know you really wanted to go to school," he said to Lungi. "But always remember the Sea Rescue lesson. If the river is flooding, don't cross it! Call an adult for help. "$$),
    ('34544', 8, $$The next day, when the river was back to normal, the children could cross it and go to school. They told the teacher what had happened.$$),
    ('34544', 9, $$"Wow! That was frightening! " said teacher. "The most important thing is that Lungi is safe. I am sure you will never try to cross a flooded river again. " "Let's talk about this in class today so everyone knows how dangerous rivers can be," added teacher as the lesson began.$$),
    ('34547', 0, $$Johnny is late to meet his friends to go fishing. When he arrives at the beach, he realises that he's forgotten to bring his lifejacket. "Don't worry," says Ben, the boat owner. "Here's a spare one I always keep on board. "$$),
    ('34547', 1, $$Because he's been fishing for years, Johnny knows the right way to put on a lifejacket. He fastens the two straps across his chest and the two straps between his legs. "Right! " he says, "it's on firmly and I'm ready to go! "$$),
    ('34547', 2, $$On the ocean, they find a good spot to fish and put down the anchor. Out of nowhere, a huge wave suddenly rises above them. "Look! The wave's going to hit us! " shouts one of the fishermen.$$),
    ('34547', 3, $$The boat is turned upside down and the men are flung into the water. "Eeeeeehhh! " they yell as they are plunged into the icy water. Not all of them can swim but, luckily, they are all wearing lifejackets.$$),
    ('34547', 4, $$The men cling to the side of the upturned boat. Ben always carries a cellphone in a plastic pouch tied to his lifejacket. He calls the free emergency number 112. "Help! We're in trouble out at sea," he says to the operator.$$),
    ('34547', 5, $$The Emergency Call Centre operator asks questions and listens carefully to Ben. She will be able to tell Sea Rescue exactly where the fishermen are.$$),
    ('34547', 6, $$The men cling to the boat in the cold water, waiting. Johnny whistles a tune to keep up their spirits. Time seems to pass slowly. But after only 20 minutes, they hear the sound of a Sea Rescue boat arriving.$$),
    ('34547', 7, $$They're here! " whoops Ben, when he sees the yellow and red Sea Rescue boat. "Yay! " the men chorus, happy to be alive.$$),
    ('34547', 8, $$Soon the fishermen are wrapped in warm blankets and the Sea Rescue boat is taking them back to the beach. "Thank goodness we were all wearing lifejackets! " says Ben.$$),
    ('34548', 0, $$If someone is in water, you can use a stick to pull the person to safety. Never get into the water to try and rescue someone. If you get into the water, you could also drown.$$),
    ('34548', 1, $$If the person who needs help is too far away from you to reach with a stick, you can throw something that floats. Throw something they can hold on to and use to stay above the water. You could throw a soccer ball or an empty five-litre plastic container.$$),
    ('34548', 2, $$If someone needs rescuing from water, ask a lifeguard or adult for help. Never go into the water to try and rescue someone yourself. You can also call the free national emergency number, 112, from a cell phone or a landline.$$),
    ('34548', 3, $$If someone is rescued from the water and they are not breathing, you should call 112 for help. You can then start Hands-on CPR by pushing hard and fast in the centre of their chest. Do not practice this on a friend! You can find out more from the National Sea Rescue Institute.$$),
    ('34549', 0, $$When going to the beach, find out which ones have lifeguards. Always try to visit beaches that have lifeguards watching the swimmers. The lifeguards on duty will put red and yellow flags on the beach to show you where it is safe to swim.$$),
    ('34549', 1, $$Many people find it hard to see a rip current in the sea. Rip currents are like fast-flowing rivers that can pull even strong swimmers away from the beach. This is why it is better to swim between the lifeguard flags.$$),
    ('34549', 2, $$If you get pulled out by a rip current, try not to panic. Try to swim to the left or to the right of the current's flow. Don't try to fight the current or to swim against the current. That will make you tired and more scared.$$),
    ('34549', 3, $$To be safe when you visit the beach, you should always listen to the lifeguards. And make sure that you stay between the red and yellow flags on the beach. The flags show you where the currents are safe.$$),
    ('34575', 0, $$Once upon a time, there lived a girl. Her parents brought her up in a presentable way, always smart and good to others. She was respectful and most of all very humble. One day as she was playing with her friends they discovered a place where$$),
    ('34575', 1, $$they could hide while playing and no one would find them. This place they found was a home for a young boy who was homeless. They found the boy asleep, shivering and hungry too. She told her other friends what she saw and they went to check$$),
    ('34575', 2, $$for themselves. She asked them to help the boy with what they had. Some brought food, clothes,water and playing items for the boy. When the boy saw all that,he became very happy and thanked them for considering him as one as their friend.$$),
    ('34575', 3, $$Months after months, the girl would bring the boy food and some water, and if sick she would stay with him till evening. One day her parents were concerned where their daughter went to in the afternoons after school.$$),
    ('34575', 4, $$They decided to follow her till where she went. On arriving she gave the boy as usual food and water but this time she came with book and read stories for him. The girl ensured the boy knew how to read and write. One day after school she took$$),
    ('34575', 5, $$extra books for her friend. She was so excited and ran to give the boy the books. That day she didn't bring him food as she was too excited about the books. They read the books and wrote suddenly, it got late as she waited for$$),
    ('34575', 6, $$the rain to go but later decided to stay there the whole night. Her parents got really worried that something terrible might have happened to their daughter so they decided to go look for her. When they arrived they found them together$$),
    ('34575', 7, $$in the cold trying to keep warm with the few clothes that the boy had. It was time for her to leave and she requested the parents to not leave the boy behind. The parents were not for the idea but the girl insisted that if the is left$$),
    ('34575', 8, $$then she would be left, the parents had no choice but to go with the boy too. The girl was really happy that the boy would now eat,bath and sleep comfortably. Early the following day, the girl asked the parents to take him to school but$$),
    ('34575', 9, $$the girl's parents declined as they didn't know the boy. The girl told them "I know him very well,I took care of him everyday after school, brought him food and taught him how to read and write. " She added,$$),
    ('34575', 10, $$"He is a good boy but has no one to take care of him. " The parents were challenged by their girl's kindness and promised to think about it. The boy stayed with them till the end of that month.$$),
    ('34575', 11, $$The following month the parents were ready to take responsibility of raising the boy as their own son. They adopted the boy,gave him a name took him to school and lived as a family. The boy was very bright in class always leading.$$),
    ('34575', 12, $$He was disciplined too and the teachers were very proud of him. He was greatful to the parents for taking him as their own son,he loved them. They lived happily as one family.$$),
    ('34577', 0, $$There was a girl called Amina. Amina had a problem with her eyesight so she used a walking stick. Amina loved staying in the garden smelling the beautiful flowers.$$),
    ('34577', 1, $$One day, Amina found the most beautiful flower in the garden. She loved its scent so much that she didn't want to leave it. She plucked the flower and held it in her hands.$$),
    ('34577', 2, $$As she was leaving the garden, she heard thunder. She knew it would rain soon. She decided to hurry home.$$),
    ('34577', 3, $$She heard more thunder and was afraid of lightning. She stopped and listened.$$),
    ('34577', 4, $$It then started raining. Amina tried to run but by bad luck, she slipped and fell.$$),
    ('34577', 5, $$Luckily, Amina's neighbours found her in the garden. They took her home and put a bandage where she was bleeding. Amina was grateful to the neighbours for their help.$$),
    ('34577', 6, $$Amina forgot about the pain she was in. She wanted her flower. Children found the flower floating in the water and brought it to Amina. Amina was very happy to have the flower back.$$),
    ('34577', 7, $$After two days, Amina felt better. She went round the garden everyday smelling more flowers.$$),
    ('34656', 0, $$Amara was walking through the park. The trees in the park were green and healthy. But, there was one tree that was brown and dry.$$),
    ('34656', 1, $$"This tree needs water," said Amara to herself. She watered the tree and it came to life with new growth. It was a magnificent green tree.$$),
    ('34656', 2, $$Then, the tree spoke! "You watered me and brought me back to life," said the tree. "I'm a magic tree, I shall grant you three wishes. "$$),
    ('34656', 3, $$Amara made her first wish. "I wish for a red bicycle," she said cautiously. Abracadabra! A red bicycle appeared.$$),
    ('34656', 4, $$She made her second wish after thinking for a few moments. "I wish for a radio," said Amara. Abracadabra! A radio appeared.$$),
    ('34656', 5, $$Amara made her third wish. "I wish for pink crystal earrings," she said happily. Abracadabra! Pink crystal earrings appeared.$$),
    ('34656', 6, $$The magic tree said, "You have everything that you wanted. " Amara smiled, "Yes I do, but those things were not for me. " The magic tree looked confused.$$),
    ('34656', 7, $$"The bicycle is for my older brother. He outgrew his bicycle. The radio is for Dad. His radio broke. The earrings are for Mum. She loves fancy earrings," explained Amara. "And they will all share with me! " she added.$$),
    ('34668', 0, $$Nina is sick . Her parents look after her often so that she can get better.@Nina is lying on her bed. Her parents are talking to her . Nina's dad asked "How are you feeling today my child ? " @Nina replied "I'm very much better dad , Thanks"$$),
    ('34668', 1, $$Nina's mother surprised Nina with a sunflower. Nina was very happy . She told her parents that she will be going to Sunflower field farm at Living Land City. Her parents agreed but they warned her that there will be a storm.$$),
    ('34668', 2, $$Nina arrived at Sunflower field farm. She enjoyed watching the flowers and also she enjoy watching the pollinators. She even forgot that there is a storm coming.$$),
    ('34668', 3, $$Nina looked and looked to the flowers. She now sees the sky that it is turning dark. She was scared. She said "The storm is coming they warned me. They warned me the storm is coming ". @Then it started raining heavily with hail.$$),
    ('34668', 4, $$Nina was now even more scared because there was a lightning. She crawled on the green grass of the field until at the gate of the farm. Sadly the gate is locked. Nina must find the way to be out of the Sunflower field.$$),
    ('34668', 5, $$Nina screamed for help at the field gate but no one responded. Nina was scared but she told her self not to worry but must be strong.$$),
    ('34668', 6, $$At home, Nina's parents are worried that Nina is not back at home and there are floods outside their house. Nina's parents waited until the storm stopped and the floods were clear so that it can be safe to look for her.$$),
    ('34668', 7, $$The storm and the floods cleared. Now Nina's parents must look for Nina .$$),
    ('34668', 8, $$At the field ,Nina thought that maybe if she runs and pushes the gate , the gate will open. Nina tried her idea. Sadly she fell and she got injured on her forehead. She cried.$$),
    ('34668', 9, $$Back at home , her parents and her brother looked for her everywhere but she was not found. Her parents asked people if they saw her and they didn't.$$),
    ('34668', 10, $$Nina's brother told her father that Nina must be at the Sunflower Field. Nina's dad said "Yes, my boy . She must be there . Let us go there "$$),
    ('34668', 11, $$They rushed there. They found her injured. Nina's father asked the security to open the Fields gate. The security said "The gate opener is at the School Uniform Shop , he will be back. " Nina's father and her brother rushed there.$$),
    ('34668', 12, $$They found the gate opener at the shop. @They arrived at the Sunflower Field and the gate was unlocked. They were very happy to see her but@sadly they found Nina injured on her forehead and her father rushed her to a local clinic.$$),
    ('34668', 13, $$They went to a local clinic . Nina was checked and was given medicine by her doctor to take at home.$$),
    ('34668', 14, $$They returned home . Nina told her parents and siblings of what happened. They forgave her.@Nina healed on her forehead.$$),
    ('34668', 15, $$Nina told herself that what she did is wrong. She told everyone in her community of what happened at the Sunflower field.$$),
    ('35033', 0, $$I wonder if there is another me.$$),
    ('35033', 1, $$That looks just like me.$$),
    ('35033', 2, $$That talks just like me.$$),
    ('35033', 3, $$That has a curly tail. Just like mine.$$),
    ('35033', 4, $$Someone with eyes and ears like mine.$$),
    ('35033', 5, $$That even laughs just like me.$$),
    ('35033', 6, $$Who can do what I can do.....$$),
    ('35033', 7, $$...and can't do what I can't do.$$),
    ('35033', 8, $$I searched everywhere. I even went to the park to look behind the big tree.$$),
    ('35033', 9, $$I looked up and down, left and right and all around.$$),
    ('35033', 10, $$I looked at every animal I could find.$$),
    ('35033', 11, $$But nowhere could I see, anybody that looked just like me.$$),
    ('35033', 12, $$I am the only me. I am very special you see.$$),
    ('35033', 13, $$But I am not the only special one. There is only one of you too!$$),
    ('35250', 0, $$Sara has a canoe to cross the river.$$),
    ('35250', 1, $$Some women want to cross.$$),
    ('35250', 2, $$Some men want to cross.$$),
    ('35250', 3, $$They get in.$$),
    ('35250', 4, $$Some animals want to cross.$$),
    ('35250', 5, $$They get in.$$),
    ('35250', 6, $$The elephant wants to cross.$$),
    ('35250', 7, $$Everyone falls out!$$),
    ('35250', 8, $$The elephant is sad.$$),
    ('35250', 9, $$Sara takes the women across.$$),
    ('35250', 10, $$She takes the men across.$$),
    ('35250', 11, $$She takes the animals across.$$),
    ('35250', 12, $$The elephant has to walk!$$),
    ('35252', 0, $$They closed the schools, and sent us home.$$),
    ('35252', 1, $$We cannot play with other children.$$),
    ('35252', 2, $$I miss being with my friends.$$),
    ('35252', 3, $$I miss going to school.$$),
    ('35252', 4, $$Mother is worried about Uncle. He is sick in hospital.$$),
    ('35252', 5, $$Our parents are worried about everything.$$),
    ('35252', 6, $$Everyone is worried about getting sick from this virus.$$),
    ('35252', 7, $$All we hear about is the coronavirus! I wish it would go away!$$),
    ('35302', 0, $$In a village called Sati Agirigi, many farmers lived in thatched huts. They also built huts as barns. They kept produce from their farms in the barns.$$),
    ('35302', 1, $$My parents, my siblings and I lived in three thatched huts, far from the farmlands. We also had a big barn for our farm produce.$$),
    ('35302', 2, $$We planted many different crops on our farm. We farmed yams, maize, cassavas, beans and groundnuts.$$),
    ('35302', 3, $$During harvest seasons, my parents and my siblings and I worked hard. We brought home the crops and put them in the barn.$$),
    ('35302', 4, $$We earn our living from our farm produce. Our mother usually takes some to sell on market days. We keep some produce for food, and planting during the next planting season.$$),
    ('35302', 5, $$One day as we planted crops on the farm, my brother's hoe handle broke. My mother sent me home to fetch another hoe from the barn.$$),
    ('35302', 6, $$When I reached home, I threw open the door of the barn. To my surprise, many rats of all sizes were running everywhere, looking for places to hide.$$),
    ('35302', 7, $$They ran into heaps of yam tubers and between stacks of bags of maize, cassava and beans. They disappeared quickly. All was quiet. I now knew why our full bags of groundnuts shrink every day.$$),
    ('35302', 8, $$When I told my father, he was not surprised. "Most of the rats come from the bush through holes in the barn walls. Rats spread diseases. That's why I always say we must cook food before eating it," he said.$$),
    ('35302', 9, $$When we came back home, we cooked. After we ate, our father explained that one of the diseases spread by rats was Lassa fever, which can cause death. Rats also carry many other serious diseases.$$),
    ('35302', 10, $$The next morning, we stayed at home. We took out all the produce from the barn and blocked the rat holes in the walls with cement.$$),
    ('35302', 11, $$We also cleared the bushes close to our home. That will help to keep the rats away from our huts and barn. Rats do not like clean, clear places.$$),
    ('35347', 0, $$One morning Mr G the goat wakes up feeling hungry.$$),
    ('35347', 1, $$At 6 o clock he eats his rope. Mr G is still hungry.$$),
    ('35347', 2, $$At 7 o clock he eats 2 socks.@Mr G is still hungry.$$),
    ('35347', 3, $$At 8 o clock he eats 3 plastic bags.@Mr G is still hungry.$$),
    ('35347', 4, $$At 9 o clock he eats 4 carrots.@Mr G is still hungry.$$),
    ('35347', 5, $$At 10 o clock he eats 5 apples.@Mr G is still hungry.$$),
    ('35347', 6, $$At 11 o clock he eats 6 biscuits.@Mr G is still hungry.$$),
    ('35347', 7, $$At midday Mr G eats an iphone, a tshirt, a flower, a rubber ball, a plastic chair, a baby tree and a bag of peanuts.$$),
    ('35347', 8, $$At 1 o clock Mr G does not feel well.$$),
    ('35347', 9, $$At 2 o clock Mr G drinks a bucket of water.$$),
    ('35347', 10, $$At 3 o clock Mr G has a sleep.$$),
    ('35347', 11, $$At 4 o clock Mr G is still asleep.$$),
    ('35347', 12, $$At 5 o clock Mr G eats his supper, some lovely Kinkeliba leaves.$$),
    ('35347', 13, $$At 6 o clock Mr G feels better.$$),
    ('35350', 0, $$It was an normal day were an coach was teaching them how to play football and some tricks to play .$$),
    ('35350', 1, $$Suddenly a chicken started to peek them behind bushes .$$),
    ('35350', 2, $$Then the coach said go run catch the chicken it can be our lunch! And then all the kids started to run !$$),
    ('35350', 3, $$And then the chicken was panicking about those kids so he did is he ran and said it to the cat so she could stay safe$$),
    ('35350', 4, $$And then the cat said " OH my God " we have to go to the dog and say him about this! And then they went and said everything to the dog .....$$),
    ('35350', 5, $$Then the dog said okay we gotta run but we have to say it to the horse too isn't ? Then all the animals said yes they went to the horse and said everything then they said now we gotta hide somewhere said teh horse 🐴 and even the others @a$$),
    ('35350', 6, $$It was night all most but then eventually they found a hut they were so happy they couldn't wait to go inside it didn't look like that there was someone inside...$$),
    ('35350', 7, $$Then they went inside and saw some food , they ate it all without even saying a word and they were really happy.$$),
    ('35350', 8, $$And then after having all the food they were happy by seeing the moon and the food...$$),
    ('35356', 0, $$Hello, I am Chicken.@What can we get from Chicken?@We can get eggs and meat.$$),
    ('35356', 1, $$Hello I am goat.@What can we get from Goat?@We can get meat, milk, cheese and wool.$$),
    ('35356', 2, $$Hello, I am cow.@What can we get from Cow?@We can get steak, cheese, milk, beef and leather.$$),
    ('35356', 3, $$Hello, I am sheep.@What can we get from Sheep.@We can get cheese, wool and lamb chops.$$),
    ('35356', 4, $$Hello, I am pig.@What can we get from Pig?@We can get bacon, pork sausages, ham and pork chops.$$),
    ('35356', 5, $$Thank you animals!$$),
    ('35392', 0, $$My name is Zadoo. I love reading storybooks. If I could visit an African Storybook storybook,$$),
    ('35392', 1, $$I would visit 'A Very Tall Man' in his very tall house in the forest. I would sit on his very tall chair and eat with his very long fork.$$),
    ('35392', 2, $$I would visit 'The Magical Rainbow River' in Mbadede, to eat the ice cream found on the river banks. I may even take a drink for healing.$$),
    ('35392', 3, $$I would visit 'Kalabushe the Talkative', and ask her to please share the recipe for her grandmother's pie. I like learning new recipes.$$),
    ('35392', 4, $$I would visit 'Abebech the Bajaj Driver' in Ethiopia. She is such an inspiration! Read her story to find out why she is inspiring.$$),
    ('35392', 5, $$I would follow the 'Busy, Busy Sun' to Terfa's compound for the recipe of bier and apukpa. I hear it is some kind of millet porridge and bambara nut pudding.$$),
    ('35392', 6, $$I would join Juma and Kadogo in the 'Africa Unity Race', a marathon to unite all African people. Maybe they would let me hold the torch of flames as we run together.$$),
    ('35392', 7, $$I would spend some time with Ayator and his friends, to learn more about how 'Emotions Come and Go'. How are you feeling right now?$$),
    ('35392', 8, $$I would join Hamisi and his father to shop for a new uniform in 'Hamisi's Lucky Day'. I like admiring new and colourful clothes at the market, and finding out prices.$$),
    ('35392', 9, $$In 'Kariza's Questions', I would join Kariza at school to also ask her teacher some questions. I would use a microscope to see the germs on my hands. I would wash the germs away with soap and water!$$),
    ('35392', 10, $$I would visit Anansi the clever spider. I want to say "thank you" to him. He did a splendid job at getting stories from the sky god Nyame, and bringing them to earth. Do you know 'How Stories Came to People'?$$),
    ('35392', 11, $$In this storybook, I took you to visit the characters and places in some of my favourite storybooks. When you next read a storybook, where will you visit and who will you meet?$$),
    ('35415', 0, $$Aisha is chuckling because she heard a funny story. She is smiling. What is Aisha feeling?$$),
    ('35415', 1, $$Isah is feeling grumpy. He has a scowl on his face. Why is he irritated?$$),
    ('35415', 2, $$Yuadoo is scared of the dark. Everyone feels fear sometimes. But Yuadoo can ask for help.$$),
    ('35415', 3, $$Chidubem is worried about his school work. He can tell his teacher. He can ask for help.$$),
    ('35415', 4, $$Lushan is playing around! It's okay to be silly sometimes.$$),
    ('35415', 5, $$Eruro is feeling sad. It's okay to cry. Emotions come and go.$$),
    ('35415', 6, $$Ayator is bursting with happiness. He is joyful. Emotions come and go.$$),
    ('35415', 7, $$Hadiza is bored. She needs to find something to do.$$),
    ('35415', 8, $$Ayo is angry. He is frustrated. Anger is a difficult feeling.$$),
    ('35415', 9, $$Labake is excited. What's the cause of her excitement? Mother made her favourite food.$$),
    ('35415', 10, $$Zege felt sleepy. He was very tired. "But wait, is 'sleepy' an emotion? " asks Efe.$$),
    ('35415', 11, $$Efe is confused! Can you answer his question?$$),
    ('35415', 12, $$Tega is feeling surprise and shock. He heard some gossip. Is it true?$$),
    ('35415', 13, $$Yebo is sick. She feels miserable. She needs some medicine and rest to feel better.$$),
    ('35415', 14, $$Sekyen is feeling content. She has finished her chores. Now she can play.$$),
    ('35415', 15, $$Bello does not have chores today. He shows two thumbs up to Sekyen. "Good job, now let's play! " he says.$$),
    ('35417', 0, $$My village had many problems. We made a long line to fetch water from one tap.$$),
    ('35417', 1, $$We waited for food donated by others.$$),
    ('35417', 2, $$We locked our houses early because of thieves.$$),
    ('35417', 3, $$Many children dropped out of school.$$),
    ('35417', 4, $$Young girls worked as maids in other villages.$$),
    ('35417', 5, $$Young boys roamed around the village while others worked on people's farms.$$),
    ('35417', 6, $$When the wind blew, waste paper hung on trees and fences.$$),
    ('35417', 7, $$People were cut by broken glass that was thrown carelessly.$$),
    ('35417', 8, $$Then one day, the tap dried up and our containers were empty.$$),
    ('35417', 9, $$My father walked from house to house asking people to attend a village meeting.$$),
    ('35417', 10, $$People gathered under a big tree and listened.$$),
    ('35417', 11, $$My father stood up and said, "We need to work together to solve our problems. "$$),
    ('35417', 12, $$Eight-year-old Aminu, sitting on a tree trunk shouted, "I can help with cleaning up. "$$),
    ('35417', 13, $$One woman said, "The women can join me to grow food. "$$),
    ('35417', 14, $$Another man stood up and said, "The men will dig a well. "$$),
    ('35417', 15, $$We all shouted with one voice, "We must change our lives. " From that day we worked together to solve our problems.$$),
    ('35419', 0, $$The wind howled like a wolf. Salamatu ran out with her kite to play.$$),
    ('35419', 1, $$The wind played with her hair. The wind played with her dress. Soon, the wind grew stronger and so she lost@her kite.$$),
    ('35419', 2, $$The wind continued to blow stronger. Salamatu ran to get the clothes from the@line.$$),
    ('35419', 3, $$The wind was faster than her. It swirled and churned. It carried her kite and clothes. It carried the house, the trees and even the leaves.$$),
    ('35419', 4, $$The wind churned and weaved them all together into a vortex.$$),
    ('35419', 5, $$Then the wind began to calm. It dropped some trees. Salamatu's kite was stuck to a branch.$$),
    ('35419', 6, $$The wind tossed her kite. It tossed some leaves around.$$),
    ('35419', 7, $$The wind dropped Salamatu from the sky along with a tree. She twirled and twirled.$$),
    ('35419', 8, $$She held on to the roots because she felt woozy,@woozy.$$),
    ('35419', 9, $$She staggered up, still holding on to the roots. She looked around for everything the wind@weaved into a vortex.$$),
    ('35419', 10, $$She saw her house. She saw a few leaves and tree trunks. She didn't see her kite but walked home all the@same.$$),
    ('35419', 11, $$Salamatu knew that the wind would blow again. "I'll see my kite again," she thought.$$),
    ('35421', 0, $$One Morning Chicken came screaming...... It has begin it has begin.... Runing straight to Rabbit sitting in the sun.$$),
    ('35421', 1, $$Rabbit got such a big fright that he also started Screaming and he and chicken ran over to the barn.$$),
    ('35421', 2, $$Near the barn Lucky the dog was sleeping in the sun. He awakes with screaming animals around him shouting it has begun, it has begun ... He also started to act crazy.$$),
    ('35421', 3, $$Chicken, Rabbit and Lucky the dog all started running screaming, it has begun it has begun.$$),
    ('35421', 4, $$They ran to the stable and Miss Horse asked: Why are you making such a noise? They all answered at the same time it has begun, it has begun .....$$),
    ('35421', 5, $$Miss Horse was so terrified about the noise that she too started yelling and joined the other crazy animals.$$),
    ('35421', 6, $$At the bottom off the road they ran into Donkey. What is the matter with you? Are you all crazy? They only shouted it has begun, it has begun...... So poor Donkey decided to join the crazy animals.$$),
    ('35421', 7, $$They ran across the field, over the hills and across the river screaming and shouting.$$),
    ('35421', 8, $$Down the medow they met Miss Cow, she looked at them and moo.... Why are you all running like crazy animals she asked? Donkey replied : I really don't know, it looked like fun running around with them.$$),
    ('35421', 9, $$Everybody stopped. Looking at each other? Donkey asks horse: Why are we running? I don't know.$$),
    ('35421', 10, $$Everybody stopped and look at chicken.@You.... What is coming? Chicken laughed, well I was playing a game with myself, I was running away from my shadow, pretending it was a monster chasing me.@Why were you also running and screaming?$$),
    ('35428', 0, $$In the farm,there lived some farm animals. Each time the farmer goes out,chaos begins to reign$$),
    ('35428', 1, $$All the animals in the farm hates each other,especially the cow$$),
    ('35428', 2, $$The animals are always running up and down, they can never rest or even sit one place$$),
    ('35428', 3, $$The animals finally became friends one day they respected each other and shares their opinion thank you for reading$$),
    ('35430', 0, $$Once upon a time there lived a boy who had long legs one day the legs put him in trouble he broke his hand when he was walking on the road he was rushed to the hospital$$),
    ('35430', 1, $$He works as a bicycle transporter all his costumers did not like his leg so they stopped using his bike he only drives his brother to school$$),
    ('35430', 2, $$He did a surgery and it was successful he had normal legs like his brother$$),
    ('35430', 3, $$Every body paid attention to him now and he lived happily ever after$$)
  ) AS v(source_id, page_index, text)
  JOIN books b
    ON b.source_platform = 'african_storybook' AND b.source_id = v.source_id
ON CONFLICT (book_id, page_index) DO NOTHING;

-- ───────── [적재검증] 트랜잭션 안 ─────────
-- (c) 적재 후 행 수 — 기대 438
SELECT count(*) AS rows_after FROM book_text bt
  JOIN books b ON b.id = bt.book_id
  WHERE b.source_platform='african_storybook' AND b.source_id IN ('33035', '33042', '33047', '33082', '33142', '33145', '33215', '33600', '33679', '33684', '33732', '33738', '33761', '33926', '33968', '34005', '34094', '34098', '34111', '34242', '34274', '34285', '34359', '34414', '34418', '34450', '34544', '34547', '34548', '34549', '34575', '34577', '34656', '34668', '35033', '35250', '35252', '35302', '35347', '35350', '35356', '35392', '35415', '35417', '35419', '35421', '35428', '35430');
-- (d) 조인 실패로 누락된 source_id — 기대 0행
SELECT v.source_id FROM (VALUES ('33035'), ('33042'), ('33047'), ('33082'), ('33142'), ('33145'), ('33215'), ('33600'), ('33679'), ('33684'), ('33732'), ('33738'), ('33761'), ('33926'), ('33968'), ('34005'), ('34094'), ('34098'), ('34111'), ('34242'), ('34274'), ('34285'), ('34359'), ('34414'), ('34418'), ('34450'), ('34544'), ('34547'), ('34548'), ('34549'), ('34575'), ('34577'), ('34656'), ('34668'), ('35033'), ('35250'), ('35252'), ('35302'), ('35347'), ('35350'), ('35356'), ('35392'), ('35415'), ('35417'), ('35419'), ('35421'), ('35428'), ('35430')) AS v(source_id)
  WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM books b
     WHERE b.source_platform='african_storybook' AND b.source_id=v.source_id);
-- (e) source 라벨 분포 — 기대 manifest_txt_v1 1종 / 438행
SELECT bt.source, count(*) FROM book_text bt JOIN books b ON b.id=bt.book_id
  WHERE b.source_platform='african_storybook' AND b.source_id IN ('33035', '33042', '33047', '33082', '33142', '33145', '33215', '33600', '33679', '33684', '33732', '33738', '33761', '33926', '33968', '34005', '34094', '34098', '34111', '34242', '34274', '34285', '34359', '34414', '34418', '34450', '34544', '34547', '34548', '34549', '34575', '34577', '34656', '34668', '35033', '35250', '35252', '35302', '35347', '35350', '35356', '35392', '35415', '35417', '35419', '35421', '35428', '35430')
  GROUP BY bt.source;
-- (f) page_index 축 검증 — 권마다 0부터 연속이어야 한다. 기대 0행(위반 없음)
SELECT b.source_id, min(bt.page_index) AS mn, max(bt.page_index) AS mx, count(*) AS n
  FROM book_text bt JOIN books b ON b.id=bt.book_id
  WHERE b.source_platform='african_storybook' AND b.source_id IN ('33035', '33042', '33047', '33082', '33142', '33145', '33215', '33600', '33679', '33684', '33732', '33738', '33761', '33926', '33968', '34005', '34094', '34098', '34111', '34242', '34274', '34285', '34359', '34414', '34418', '34450', '34544', '34547', '34548', '34549', '34575', '34577', '34656', '34668', '35033', '35250', '35252', '35302', '35347', '35350', '35356', '35392', '35415', '35417', '35419', '35421', '35428', '35430')
  GROUP BY b.source_id HAVING min(bt.page_index) <> 0 OR max(bt.page_index) <> count(*)-1;
-- (g) 빈 면 행 수 — 기대 0 (D7: 빈 면도 text='' 로 적재)
SELECT count(*) AS empty_rows FROM book_text bt JOIN books b ON b.id=bt.book_id
  WHERE b.source_platform='african_storybook' AND b.source_id IN ('33035', '33042', '33047', '33082', '33142', '33145', '33215', '33600', '33679', '33684', '33732', '33738', '33761', '33926', '33968', '34005', '34094', '34098', '34111', '34242', '34274', '34285', '34359', '34414', '34418', '34450', '34544', '34547', '34548', '34549', '34575', '34577', '34656', '34668', '35033', '35250', '35252', '35302', '35347', '35350', '35356', '35392', '35415', '35417', '35419', '35421', '35428', '35430') AND bt.text = '';

